Conditional Humana BO Approval Requirements

DR (Disaster Recovery)
Release deployments (for example, 2026R4 release code): The Humana approval provided for promotion to Production will also satisfy the approval requirement for deployment to DR.
Nothing should be going to DR that is not in production.
HTFX
Release deployments (for example, 2026R4 release code): The Humana approval provided for promotion to Production will also satisfy the approval requirement for deployment to HTFX.
Defect fixes deployed directly to HTFX: Humana BO approval is required prior to CCB approval/ deployment.
HUAT
Release deployments (for example, 2026R4 release code): Humana BO approval is not required.
Defect fixes (whether deployed during a UAT testing window or on an ad hoc basis), as well as any code promoted to HUAT outside of the scheduled release process, will require Humana BO approval prior to CCB approval/ deployment.
 
Note: Humana approval only applies to tickets with Humana impact or the potential for Humana impact. For deployments that only impact SS&C there is no need for Humana approval in any environment.
 
Approval Process
As a short-term solution, approvals should be obtained via email to the appropriate Humana Business Owner (BO), with a copy sent to release_oversight@sscinc.com.
The subject line of the email should state:
Formal Migration Approval Request for installing <JIRA ticket> to <environment>
Example: Formal Migration approval Request for installing ADJCOM-xxxxx to HUAT
 if approval is being sought on multiple tickets in a single request, indicate “multiple tickets” in the subject line and list the tickets in the body of the email.
If the appropriate Humana BO is not known, please indicate that in your approval request. The Release Oversight team will assist in identifying the correct approver.
Once the required approvals are received:
The Release Oversight team will document the approval in Jira, including:
The name of the approving Humana BO
Release Oversight approval
This approval documentation must be completed before a CCB request is submitted.
The approval email should be attached to the CCB request as supporting documentation.
Note: This process is intended to be temporary while we evaluate and implement more automated approval workflows. 
 
This process closely mirrors the process currently in place for the RxNova environments, which will also no longer require executive approval for deployment and will be returned to the established processes.
 
If you have any questions regarding this change or the updated approval requirements, please contact release_oversight@sscinc.com.
 
